&lt;p style="font: 10.5pt Arial, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 12pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0pt"&gt;&lt;font style="color: #110C16"&gt;The
Company &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #26212A"&gt;has &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #110C16"&gt;a revolving line of credit agreement with US Bank
&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #26212A"&gt;providing &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #110C16"&gt;the Company with &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #26212A"&gt;loans
&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #110C16"&gt;up to $3,000,000 on a revolving &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #26212A"&gt;basis &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #110C16"&gt;with
a maturity date of October 29, 2026. Interest is payable monthly at rates established by US Bank, which &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #26212A"&gt;is
&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #110C16"&gt;based on an annual &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #26212A"&gt;rate &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #110C16"&gt;equal
to 2.0%&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="color: #26212A"&gt;plus&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="color: #110C16"&gt;the one-month SOFR rate quoted by Bank from Reuters
Screen. The rate was 5.87% and 6.55% at December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 10.5pt Arial, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 12pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0pt"&gt;&lt;font style="color: #110C16"&gt;The
Company &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #26212A"&gt;has &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #110C16"&gt;an additional revolving line of credit agreement with
National Bank of Commerce &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #26212A"&gt;providing &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #110C16"&gt;the Company with &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #26212A"&gt;loans
&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #110C16"&gt;up to $2,000,000 on a revolving basis with a maturity date of July 5, 2026. Interest is payable monthly
at rates established by National Bank of Commerce, which is based on the Prime Rate as published in the &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #26212A"&gt;"Money
&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #110C16"&gt;Rates" section of the Wall Street Journal. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #26212A"&gt;The rate &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="color: #110C16"&gt;was
6.75% and 7.50% at December 31, 2025 and 2024, &lt;font style="letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;respectively.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 10.5pt Arial, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; text-indent: 0pt; margin: 0pt 0pt 12pt"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 10.5pt Arial, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 12pt"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

